.TH LLMFS 4
.SH NAME
llmfs \- interface to LLM file system
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B llmfs
[
.B -D
] [
.BI -m " mntpt"
] [
.BI -k " apikey"
] [
.BI -M " model"
]
.PP
.B /n/llm/clone
.br
.B /n/llm/info
.br
.BI /n/llm/ n /ctl
.br
.BI /n/llm/ n /data
.br
.BI /n/llm/ n /status
.br
.BI /n/llm/ n /chat/system
.br
.BI /n/llm/ n /chat/user
.br
.BI /n/llm/ n /chat/assistant
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Llmfs
provides a way to interact with an LLM over a filesystem interface.
It serves its hierarchy on
.I mntpt
(default
.BR /n/llm ),
issuing requests to the OpenRouter chat completions API
.RB ( https://openrouter.ai/api/v1/chat/completions ).
The
.B -D
option enables Styx server tracing.
.B -M
sets the default model used for new connections
(default
.BR openai/gpt-4.1-nano ).
.B -k
supplies the OpenRouter API key;
if absent, the key is read from
.BR /env/OPENROUTER_API_KEY .
.PP
The top of the hierarchy contains a
.B clone
file, an
.B info
file and zero or more numbered directories.
Each numbered directory represents a distinct connection to the LLM
and contains the files
.BR ctl ,
.BR data ,
.BR status ,
and a
.B chat
subdirectory used as described below.
Opening the
.B clone
file reserves a connection: it is equivalent to opening the
.B ctl
file of an unused connection directory, creating a new one if necessary.
.PP
The file
.B ctl
controls a connection.
When read, it returns the decimal number
.I n
of its connection directory.
Thus, opening and reading
.B clone
allocates a connection directory and reveals the number of the allocated directory,
allowing the other files to be named (eg,
.BI /n/llm/ n /data\fR).
.PP
.B Ctl
accepts the following textual commands:
.TP
.BI "temp " n
Set the sampling temperature to
.IR n ,
a real number (typically between 0 and 2).
Issue this request before starting a prompt.
.TP
.BI "top " n
Set nucleus sampling probability
.RI ( top_p )
to
.IR n ,
a real between 0 and 1.
.TP
.BI "max_tokens " n
Limit the number of tokens to generate to
.IR n .
.TP
.BI "seed " n
Set the seed for sampling.
.TP
.BI "model " name
Override the model used for this connection (eg,
.BR anthropic/claude-sonnet-4.5 ).
.TP
.BI "mode " stream|block
Accepted for compatibility but ignored:
responses are always delivered in a single block when generation completes.
.TP
.B reset
Return the connection to the idle state, clearing any
system, user, data, and assistant content accumulated so far.
.PP
The
.B data
file provides a connection to the raw input and output of the LLM.
It must be opened separately for reading and for writing.
Writing to
.B data
appends to a plain prompt; closing the writer starts generation.
Reading
.B data
returns the generated text once generation completes;
reads issued while generation is in progress block until it finishes.
.PP
The
.B chat
directory is a structured alternative for instruction or chat models.
Writing to
.B chat/system
sets the system prompt.
Writing to
.B chat/user
sets the user message; closing the writer submits the chat and
makes the model's reply available in the read-only file
.BR chat/assistant .
As with
.BR data ,
reads on
.B chat/assistant
block until generation completes.
Writes that start at offset 0 replace the previous contents of
.B chat/system
or
.BR chat/user ;
later writes append.
.PP
Once started, a request runs until the API returns a response or an error;
closing all files for a connection abandons interest in the result.
.PP
The read-only
.B status
file provides a single word giving the state of the connection:
.BR Idle ,
.BR Prompting ,
.BR Generating ,
or
.BR Done .
.PP
The read-only
.B info
file gives basic metadata about the default model.
.SH SOURCE
.B llmfs.b
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR styxservers (2),
.IR mhttp (2)
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
A
.B write
to
.B ctl
returns with an error and sets the error string if
a command is malformed or unknown.
A
.B read
from
.B data
or
.B chat/assistant
returns an error if the upstream API call fails;
the error text describes the failure (HTTP status, dial error, or parse error).
.SH BUGS
The
.B mode
command is silently ignored; streaming output is not implemented.
